From: ARQUITECTURA (Claude) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] FlyWeb ui/gl: allow ANGLE OpenGL as a fallback before
 macOS 11

ANGLE refuses its Metal backend by machine model (MacBookPro < 13,1,
MacBookAir and Macmini < 8,1, MacBook < 9,1, iMac < 17,1), on GPU family 1
and on NVIDIA. Chromium 156 only allows ANGLE Metal on Mac, so on those
machines the GPU process cannot start and everything falls back to
software, with no WebGL.

Allow ANGLE OpenGL again, after Metal. The EGL display list
(gl_display_initializer.cc) tries Metal first and OpenGL only when the
Metal display fails to initialize, so machines where Metal works are not
affected. Limited to macOS < 11, where the hardware GL GPU mode exists
(IsMacOSBelow11()); on macOS 11+ nothing changes.

Written on paper, not compiled. Needs the IOSurface rectangle texture
target (patches 2-5, from flynk-b1b) to paint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc b/ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc
--- a/ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc
+++ b/ui/gl/init/gl_factory_mac.cc
@@ -26,6 +26,14 @@ namespace init {
 std::vector<GLImplementationParts> GetAllowedGLImplementations() {
   std::vector<GLImplementationParts> impls;
   impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kMetal);
+  // FlyWeb: ANGLE OpenGL as a fallback where ANGLE refuses Metal (machine
+  // model, GPU family 1, NVIDIA). Kept after Metal: the EGL display list tries
+  // Metal first and OpenGL only if the Metal display fails to initialize.
+  // Only before macOS 11, where the hardware GL GPU mode exists
+  // (features::IsMacOSBelow11()); on macOS 11+ nothing changes.
+  if (base::mac::MacOSVersion() < 11'00'00) {
+    impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kOpenGL);
+  }
   impls.emplace_back(gl::ANGLEImplementation::kSwiftShader);
   return impls;
 }
